; Blit the room's tile-index map ($F800) onto the real screen
;
; Used by the routine at #R$9880.
;
; .
;
; HL counts 0-511 (32x16 tile positions, matching the $F800 map size - loop
; exit checks BIT 1,H, i.e. stops once H=2). For each tile: reads the tile
; index from ($F800+HL), looks it up in a 256-byte table at $DF00 to get an
; attribute byte, writes that to the attribute file ($5800 + ...); then looks
; up an 8-byte bitmap at ($5B72)+tile_index*8 and copies it to the real screen
; bitmap address, one byte per pixel row (INC D each line - standard
; screen-third stride).
